 represents the usual formulas for changing from polar to Cartesian coordinates. \n\nTherefore, the pre-image $Δ$ of $D$ under the action of $T$ is the region that can be written as \n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 3,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\le v\\le \\frac{5\\pi }{4}}.\n$$\n\nThis is the rectangular region enclosed between\n\n- two vertical lines with Cartesian equations $u=1$ and $u=3,$ and\n\n- two horizontal lines with Cartesian equations $v=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ and $v=\\frac{5\\pi }{4},$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/5c5f652a4324d6d2ee99d5dcf5d5f3d7be69fd794ebfcd8b6b0a9300d39dca20.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/state.json" "file_sha256" "7514841bab25e28fa54563ba7ce72b6b8a8ea77b5729d54494a380b378b1e7b9"} {"question" "q-161161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2d0b12b354212cb5afd066e632738204f9acafb010ccb8683e448c306ff5704c"} {"question" "q-161161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/state.json" "file_sha256" "7514841bab25e28fa54563ba7ce72b6b8a8ea77b5729d54494a380b378b1e7b9"} {"question" "q-161161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/5a3cbfd206d61ba02ca76f28ee191dc93175f3700cc7034e352dcfaa933940c0.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question